<!--
  Only the routes that are actually public and meant to be indexed —
  everything else (Dashboard, Goals, Calendar, /ai, /analytics, etc.) sits
  behind ProtectedRoute and a logged-out visitor (Googlebot included) sees
  the Landing page instead via HomeGate, so there's nothing there for a
  crawler to index anyway. /login, /forgot-password and /reset-password
  are left out on purpose too: they're transactional, not content, and
  reset-password carries a one-time token in its query string.

  /welcome is left out too: it renders the same page as "/" (its canonical
  points there), so listing both only creates a duplicate.

  Update "lastmod" when a page's actual content changes, not on every
  deploy — it's a hint to crawlers about freshness, not a build timestamp.
-->
